  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The federal government faces $288B in contract value with periods of performance ending within the next 12 months. The largest single expiring contract is NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC, $44.1B. Other major expirations include CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC, $35.2B and THE BOEING COMPANY, $32B. Contracts ending within the window cover a mix of national lab management, defense platforms, and major services agreements. Expiring values cluster unevenly across quarters, with Apr-Jun 2027 showing $83.1B and Jul-Sep 2027 showing $120B. The dataset reports award values as total contract values for contracts whose period of performance ends within the next 12 months. End dates can be extended by options and modifications, so listed values reflect total award amounts, not single-year obligations. Companies with multiple sizable expirations include THE BOEING COMPANY, with entries at $32B and $18.1B, and major defense and nuclear site managers such as SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC, $28B, and LOCKHEED MARTIN SERVICES, LLC, $20.6B. Review upcoming procurements in the Apr-Jun 2027 and Jul-Sep 2027 windows for the largest recompete activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which contracts are the largest expirations by November 2027?",
        "body": "NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC is the single largest expiring contract at $44.1B. CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC and THE BOEING COMPANY follow at $35.2B and $32B respectively. The list also includes SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC, $28B, and LOCKHEED MARTIN SERVICES, LLC, $20.6B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "When do most of these contract expirations fall within the next 12 months?",
        "body": "Expiring contract value is concentrated in Apr-Jun 2027 and Jul-Sep 2027, with $83.1B and $120B respectively. Earlier quarters show smaller totals, including Oct-Dec 2026 at $36.3B and Jan-Mar 2027 at $45.5B, and Oct-Dec 2027 at $3B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Which large federal contracts are expiring soon?",
      "a": "Large federal contracts expiring soon include NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC, $44.1B; CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC, $35.2B; THE BOEING COMPANY, $32B and $18.1B; SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC, $28B; LOCKHEED MARTIN SERVICES, LLC, $20.6B; and others listed such as BELL BOEING JOINT PROJECT OFFICE, $7B and CHEMONICS INTERNATIONAL, INC., $6.7B. These contracts represent the largest total contract values with periods of performance ending within the next 12 months."
    },
    {
      "q": "What is a contract recompete?",
      "a": "A contract recompete is the process the government uses to re-solicit work when a contract’s period of performance ends and the agency seeks to award the work again through competition or a new award. Recompetes can follow the current contractor’s performance period and can include option years or modifications."
    },
    {
      "q": "How current is this recompete data?",
      "a": "This recompete data covers FY2027 to date. The note clarifies that award value figures are total contract values for contracts whose period of performance ends within the next 12 months and that end dates can be extended by options and modifications."
    }
  ],
